# Story: a newcomer docks three windows, frames one, wanders off, loses track of the others, and
# finds that every way back works: the frame shortcut again, home, pause, and float-all.
# Reference: T17 T30 T32 T61 T62, A40 A41. Window ids start at 101.
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
open Slack
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
# Slack (104) floats on the Desktop between them.
expect floating 104
expect count docked 3
# ⌃⌥↩ frames the focused window; the same keys again return to where the view came from.
focus 103
zoom
expect fills 103
expect hidden 101
expect hidden 104
zoom
expect camera root
expect visible 101
expect visible 104
# Wandering: frame Mail, walk to its neighbour, step in where there is nothing to step into.
zoom 102
neighbor down
expect camera 103
in
expect fail
# Lost. home shows everything.
home
expect ok
expect camera root
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
# A call starts. Framed on Notes, pause brings every window into view and Arbor lets go.
zoom 103
expect hidden 101
pause
expect ok
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 104
dock 104 left
expect fail
# Mail is closed during the call. Afterwards the arrangement and the view come back without it.
close 102
resume
expect ok
expect camera 103
expect fills 103
expect hidden 101
expect count docked 2
# Enough: back to a normal Mac.
float-all
expect ok
expect count docked 0
expect visible 101
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
